# Every file is checked out exactly as committed, on every platform. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout -- and the tests read their inputs byte
# for byte: the .pure corpus (parser parity is byte-exact), the generated files (each diff-tested
# against its generator), the goldens. Nor are endings normalized on commit: a few committed files
# carry CRLF or mixed endings (core's prelude.pure among them), and normalizing would change them.
* -text
